<title>INDIA: India's Hero Honda 96/97 net 503.6 million rupees.</title>
<headline>India's Hero Honda 96/97 net 503.6 million rupees.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	 503.6 vs   263.4</p>
<p>    Net sales	7,679.2 vs 6,319.6</p>
<p>    Div (rupees)	 3.5 vs     3.2</p>
<p>    shr (rupees)     25.22 vs    13.19</p>
<p>    Other income     149.2 vs   102.3</p>
<p>    Expenditure    6,958.1 vs 5,836.5</p>
<p>    Interest	    86.8 vs    58.8</p>
<p>    Depreciation     132.3 vs   107.2</p>
<p>    Tax		  147.5 vs   156.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Leading Indian motorcycle maker Hero Honda Motors Ltd is a joint venture between India's Hero group, controlled by the Munjal family, and Japan's Honda Motor Co.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that its board recommended a dividend of 3.50 rupees per 10-rupee share, of which 1.50 rupees has already been paid as interim dividend. The firm's higher profit was mainly due to indigenisation and a favourable exchange rate, it said. The firm said its exports grew 35 percent, but gave no details.</p>
<p>--  New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
